    "body": "## Parent\n\n#172\n\n## What to build\n\nMake Google Tasks an independently enabled Google surface with least-privilege authorization, Google Task List selection, local-first external creation, and one provider-neutral External Task Link per Task.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Other Google capabilities remain usable without the Google Tasks scope.\n- [ ] The Tasks scope is requested only when the owner enables Google Tasks as a Task Destination.\n- [ ] Permission denial or disablement leaves other Google surfaces connected and local Tasks usable.\n- [ ] The owner can select and validate a Google Task List destination.\n- [ ] A local Task commits before Google creation and retains waiting or failed link state if Google fails.\n- [ ] A Task can have at most one External Task Link, and successful creation stores provider identity, destination, remote ID, URL, and synchronization baseline.\n- [ ] Connection and creation do not import unrelated Google Tasks.\n- [ ] `npm run check` is green.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #174 — Edit Task details and organize Task Lists",
